WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.160
- Welcome to another coffee break

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.260
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.150
You know that this is the
place where I want to help you

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.570
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.160
And today's topic is a fan favorite.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.530
It's a topic that many of
you have already requested

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.950
and this is the famous
dreaded consulting bag.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.250
How do you pack your bag as a consultant?

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.170
This is what we're going to discuss today.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.300
I will show you how I packed my bag

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.670
as a consultant in the past.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.000
And I will share some tricks

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.500
which are my perspective,
what you will likely need,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.230
what you probably won't need

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.940
and probably what can be a life
saver in certain situations.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.600
So before we dive into it,
let me start by providing

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.060
some context. So as
you know if you've seen

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.040
some other videos on my
channel, the typical work week

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.840
in the life of a consultant is that

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.990
from Monday to Thursday
you're at the client.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.330
So usually Monday morning,
you take the first flight

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.140
in the morning, to fly out,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.940
fly to the client then you
fly back Thursday evening.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.380
And this, for this reason,
requires you of course

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.910
to have a well packed bag
to live through the week.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.400
Of course, at the moment,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.480
due to the current health situation,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.130
the rhythm looks a bit different.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.820
Travel is down, people are
not traveling that much.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.050
There's more home office.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.740
They also know that travel is already

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.040
starting to pick up again slowly.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.100
So trust that this will
become more relevant

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.670
for you in the future again.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.880
So let's start by talking
about the exterior

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.150
because there are some little things

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.350
that you can do as well.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.340
And one of the main problems
that you will face is,

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.530
that many, many consultants
will use very similar bags..

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.470
So at the airport, there were lots of bags

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.540
that pretty much looked the same.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.980
So my tip is , use something like this,

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.300
a little piece of something
just to mark your bag

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.436
that everybody knows that this is yours.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.180
And that you can quickly distinguish it

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.330
from other bags as well.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.540
And of course a proper luggage
tag with the information,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.390
with your personal details will be helpful

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:55.170
So that in case you lose
it, in case somebody else

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.220
finds this, they know who you are

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.860
and how they can reach you.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.880
So why do consultants
even care so much what

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.660
exactly they pack into their bag?

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.020
And the main reason is,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.000
that you will not check your luggage,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.100
so you can only bring hand luggage.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.750
and the reason is that it
would just take too much time

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.380
if after you land, you go
to the luggage bed conveyor.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.810
You wait for your piece
of baggage to pick it up.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.960
The team wants to directly take the taxi,

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.240
take the cab to the client once you land.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.330
So everybody would just
pick up hand luggage.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.870
There will be no checked in luggage.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.050
So let's start how these
bags are structured.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.990
And of course the
different types of luggages

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:29.940
will be different.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.130
But usually it'll have
one compartment where

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.270
it's more free float, right?

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.650
And one compartment that
you have a fixed thing

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.950
that you can make over it to
really keep it all in place.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.580
And I like to have the things

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.700
which are a bit more
delicate like the shirts

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.560
where you don't wanna
have too many wrinkles

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.310
after you iron them to have
them rather in this part,

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.650
because this is then how
you keep it all together

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.550
how you make sure that it's all in it.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.640
So let's start indeed with the shirts.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.960
And here what you need to understand

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.380
is that on Monday morning,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.370
you will already drive to the client

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.460
and then fly to the client fully dressed.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.740
So in your suit, in your shirt and so on.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.160
So from Monday, you
already wear your outfit.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.880
This means that you still need outfits

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.750
for Tuesday, Wednesday,
and Thursday, so three days

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.260
but then it's a good
best practice to always

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.780
have an additional one in store with you.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.840
So that for instance,
if for whatever reason,

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.913
you might need to stay there
for another day spontaneously,

00:03:19.913 --> 00:03:21.440
that you would be able to stay there

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.120
for instance on Friday as well,

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.570
without running out of cloth.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:28.520
So it's best practice to really
have four clothes with you.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.123
Four pieces of shirts, and of
course here types of shirts

00:03:31.123 --> 00:03:34.160
you see here, so I might make
another video in the future

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.920
talking a bit more about the
stupid consultant outfit.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.040
What types of shorts,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.490
what types of suits
you're supposed to wear,

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.360
but like usual plain colors,

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.790
white, blue, some simple stripes.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.150
This is what's usually, okay

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.130
this is what you were
wearing most of the time.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.690
So let's start with them indeed.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:52.330
And of course here, the critical
thing is how you fold them

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.960
because you wanna make
sure that they're not

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.200
too wrinkled when you then
unpack them in the hotel.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.409
So simple way of doing
it after you iron is

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:03.700
do it like this, put
these arms here together

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.963
and then fold it once like
this to have such a package.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.570
Then I take this package

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:14.980
and try to fit this into this half here.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.740
And you know, you might do some
delicate additional folding.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:23.740
Just of course, the less folding
you do the better for this

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.140
in order to fit this in properly.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.800
The next item to take
care of is your underwear

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.010
And here for the same logic,

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.650
you already wear your things on Monday.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.600
They don't need four more days
to be covered until Friday.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.660
And then my recommendation
is to bring even

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.920
one additional one in case
you want to do some sports.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.320
So for instance, one pair of sports socks

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.440
this always makes sense.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.230
So you have five additional
pieces of underwear.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.050
Now, if you look here in the compartment

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.560
where we put the shirts,
here it makes sense

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.930
to then staff this a little
bit here in the free spaces,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:55.923
because this will then have

00:04:55.923 --> 00:04:58.180
this whole area not to move so much.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.640
And the less, it all
moves, the less wrinkles,

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.260
the less problems you get

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.123
with ironing your shirts afterwards.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.270
So once you've all put it in,

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.920
then you can close this

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.730
and this then should make sure

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.003
that this is more or less firmly secured.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.000
And then this first half
part of the bag is done.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.950
Once you then unpack
your bag in the hotel,

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.520
it always makes sense to check

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.360
how wrinkly your shirts really are.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.030
And indeed most business
hotels will have opportunity

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.950
to helping them with the
ironing or to provide you

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.820
the facilities so that you
can then iron the shirts

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.900
in the perfect way

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.820
if they are too wrinkly
for you to wear them.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.410
Next point is the shoes.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:39.060
And this is always a question
of personal philosophy

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.020
because indeed in such a bag
you usually only have place

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.290
for one additional pair of shoes.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.000
So you really already wear
your business shoes on Monday.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.177
So the question is what is the
second pair that you bring?

00:05:49.177 --> 00:05:50.610
And some colleagues like to bring

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.860
a second pair of business shoes

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.690
so that then they can alternate
the shoes during the week.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.610
This of course can make a lot of sense

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.880
and will help you to really keep the shoes

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.420
in a well looking place for the long term.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.140
Personally I always liked
to prioritize sports.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.750
So I always brought a
pair of running shoes

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.140
so that I have these with me.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.183
And this is then indeed something

00:06:10.183 --> 00:06:13.950
that you can just then
pack in the second half.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.010
They usually did it in some way like this

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.210
to have the shoes in here in the section.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.140
I often frankly also use
the shoe bag to make sure

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:24.220
that then the potentially dirty shoes

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.390
are not making other
things dirty here as well.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.750
So for the sake of simplicity,
I'm not having these here

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.740
but indeed, you could pack
these actually in a simple

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.580
garbage bag, a simple plastic
garbage bag, for instance,

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.410
to have this clean and secured here.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.180
Next is a leisure outfit.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.770
This is a little bit optional.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.860
Not all colleagues do this,
but sometimes it can be nice.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.510
And this is for some
evenings with your colleagues

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:47.510
or maybe it's nice to go to
the hotel first to change

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.880
to then not keep continuing
wearing your dress

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.850
shirt that you wear all day from work.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:54.870
But here indeed, most
colleagues, will do this anyway

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.650
so it's not absolutely required

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.220
but sometimes it's nice
just to have a normal pair

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:02.380
of trousers and just a normal
polo shirt or something

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.110
like this that you can, wear
and do not need to walk around

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.770
with your business outfit all the time.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:08.750
So this is something that
you can just put in here

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.220
to make this work for you.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.840
The next one is your sports outfit.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.310
So we already have the shoes

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.500
and the running socks in the bag.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.690
Now, of course, a pair

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:19.790
of running trousers and then a
running short will be helpful

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.460
and appreciated depending
on the spot that you do,

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.500
you of course might also
be taking other materials

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.560
that you need to make this work for you.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:30.150
Next one is something
to keep you a bit warm

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.090
And here most people either
have an additional jumper

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:36.340
that they take with them, or
maybe also a vest like this.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.680
So often there's not
enough space to take both.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.450
Personally. I'd like to
have something like this.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.283
It's a vest.

00:07:41.283 --> 00:07:42.150
This is always nice.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.480
And you can also wear it

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.490
in the team room under
your suit, for instance.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:48.630
So this is always a nice addition

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:52.170
that's often worthwhile just
to pack and to have with you

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.310
when you pack your back.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:54.810
Next one is ties.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.750
So these days you do not need
to wear a tie at every client,

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.370
but there are still some clients
that we require you to wear

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.690
around where this is just
part of the dress code.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.770
You'll just got to have
selection of basic colors

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:07.690
nothing too crazy, like
dark blue, red green.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.750
These are colors that I
personally like to wear.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.600
And here indeed, if you know
that you will need a tie,

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.280
then pack enough, make
sure that you have three

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:17.020
or four that you can really
alternate during the week.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.400
But even if you had a client
where you do not expect

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.233
that you need to wear a tie where you know

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.340
that you actually don't need to do that.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:25.460
It's always good practice to
have at least one tie with you.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.300
So if in case maybe you are
suddenly meeting somebody else,

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.490
as a senior person, maybe also
outside of the organization

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.130
on a short notice, need
to join another workshop.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.360
Another pitch, maybe
even have another client

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.510
that you are flexible, that
you have a tie with you

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:39.550
that you can wear.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:42.230
This is then required for
the setting that you're in.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.750
And here often it's good
just to roll it a bit

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.130
make sure that you don't need it to hurt,

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.490
but a simple roll like this is
fine where then I can put it

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:52.430
in the bag and make this
work in a proper way.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.880
And last but not least your toilet bag

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.010
with all the sanitary things that you need

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.770
during your stay in the hotel.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:01.140
So here, the good thing is
if you're missing something

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.520
you forgot something at home,

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.590
most of these business hotels
will be able to provide you

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:08.400
with all the basic
things like a toothpaste

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.590
for instance, but it's
of course always nicer to

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:13.160
have your own things
that you can then bring.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.020
So indeed, I would just
always also pack it here

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.170
to the side and make sure that

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.060
it doesn't interfere
too much with your ties.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.410
And then these days, of course,

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.090
some additional corona masks.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.850
It's always helpful to
have these in the bag

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:26.380
as well to then have it
here when you need it.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:28.170
So these are all the essentials indeed.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.650
After you have all this,
you can pick it up,

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:32.320
make sure it all fits well.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:36.940
And you see this nicely fits
out, such a hand luggage.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.950
This is now also a small size these days.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.320
They're even a bit larger sizes

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.940
of hand luggage that are
allowed to be brought

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.700
into the cabin of the airplane.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:50.370
So this is fine to see that
you can easily close this.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.120
So that's it, and from my experience,

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:54.110
this is the setup that works really well.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.100
This is how I did it most of the time.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:59.337
Some colleagues like
to bring a second suit.

00:09:59.337 --> 00:10:00.303
And here the rationale is,

00:10:00.303 --> 00:10:02.150
well if you only have one suit with you

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:03.670
that you are wearing on Monday, of course,

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.503
you're risking it there,

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.640
maybe you spill some coffee over it.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.120
Maybe your trousers have some problem.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.260
That's maybe a damage
maybe they'll rip apart.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.720
And then of course you
have quite some problems.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.700
If then you have nothing
else to wear anymore.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.880
This is now one of the
reasons why some people like

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.670
to bring a second suit.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:20.503
And then ,of course,

00:10:20.503 --> 00:10:22.760
you can bring a simple suit bag like this,

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.730
this works that you can
then often put it together.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.108
You can then carry it.

00:10:27.108 --> 00:10:29.210
And then you can also have
it here around the bag.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:32.310
If you then travel around
the airport, this can work.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.250
And if you have this,
the additional benefit

